Subject: [PATCH 9/9] staging: wire in the prima WLAN driver

The two lines that make drivers/staging build prima, exactly as LineageOS'
kenzo kernel has them. The driver itself is not in this patch: it is 28 MB,
and tools/setup-kernel.sh fetches drivers/staging/prima from kenzo at a
pinned commit before the patches are applied.

prima is Qualcomm's driver for the WCNSS Pronto WLAN core in this SoC. ASUS
built it out of tree as wlan.ko from sources they did not publish, and that
module will not load on a kernel we build. Built in instead, it starts when
the WiFi HAL writes "sta" to /sys/module/wlan/parameters/fwpath.

PRONTO_WLAN is the option the defconfig sets; PRIMA_WLAN is the same driver
for the older Riva core, kept as kenzo has it.
---
diff --git drivers/staging/Kconfig drivers/staging/Kconfig
index 25c8bffd..544bec36 100644
--- drivers/staging/Kconfig
+++ drivers/staging/Kconfig
@@ -136,4 +136,6 @@ source "drivers/staging/netlogic/Kconfig"
 
 source "drivers/staging/dwc2/Kconfig"
 
+source "drivers/staging/prima/Kconfig"
+
 endif # STAGING
diff --git drivers/staging/Makefile drivers/staging/Makefile
index 57e5076f..88544b08 100644
--- drivers/staging/Makefile
+++ drivers/staging/Makefile
@@ -59,3 +59,5 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_FIREWIRE_SERIAL)	+= fwserial/
 obj-$(CONFIG_ZCACHE)		+= zcache/
 obj-$(CONFIG_GOLDFISH)		+= goldfish/
 obj-$(CONFIG_USB_DWC2)		+= dwc2/
+obj-$(CONFIG_PRIMA_WLAN)	+= prima/
+obj-$(CONFIG_PRONTO_WLAN)	+= prima/
